<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Istämi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Istämi was a Turkic ruler who governed the western part of the Gokturk realm in the sixth century CE, brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bumin-qaghan">Bumin</a>, founder of the khaganate. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muqan-qaghan">Muqan Qaghan</a> he drove westward past the Caspian into former Hephthalite territory. His campaigns extended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Gokturk Empire</a> across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and brought contact with the Byzantine world.</p></div>
